WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  A pure presentational leaf fed `motorLatest: MotorSnapshot | null` and `isolationResistance?` props by its
  parent (the drivetrain-health page). Regions inside a GlassPanel titled <Cog/> "Live Motor Status":
    • hasData (motorLatest != null):
        - Grid(2/4): four boxes — Shift State (cyan), Power (purple, "{fmtNumber} kW"), Regen (green,
          "{fmtNumber} kW"), Source (text-primary); each `value != null ? … : '—'`.
        - Grid(2/3/4): nine <InlineMetric> — Front/Rear Motor RPM (Activity, "{fmtInt} RPM"),
          Front/Rear Torque (Zap, "{fmtNumber} Nm"), Front/Rear Motor Temp + Inverter Temp + Battery Temp
          (Thermometer, "{fmtNumber(convertTempFromSI(c))} {tempUnit}"), HV Isolation (Shield, dynamic tint,
          "{fmtNumber} kΩ" when >0 else '—').
    • else: <EmptyState message="No live motor telemetry yet" />.
  Only the four temperatures are unit-converted (convertTempFromSI: °C identity, °F = c*9/5+32) then
  fmtNumber (global precision 2); power/regen/torque/isolation use fmtNumber(2); rpm uses fmtInt(0). All
  formatters apply the web `safeNumber` guard (non-finite → 0). HV-isolation icon tint ladder:
  null/≤0 → muted, ≥500 → green, ≥100 → amber, else → red.
  Data sources: useTranslation + useUnits. No data hooks at the leaf (loading/error/stale/offline are owned
  by the parent surface); the native surface reproduces those as its own state-holder lifecycle.

